  "faq": [
    {
      "question": "What is Matunga known for?",
      "answer": "Matunga is famous as Mumbai's iconic South Indian cultural hub - home to legendary udipi restaurants, the Asthika Samaj, Five Gardens, King's Circle (Maheshwari Udyan), top colleges like Ruia, Podar, VJTI and ICT, and a heritage mix of Tamil, Gujarati and Parsi communities in elegant Art Deco buildings."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the pin code of Matunga?",
      "answer": "Matunga has multiple pin codes: 400019 (Matunga East / Central), 400016 (Matunga Road / Matunga West side), and 400022 (King's Circle / Sion border belt)."
    },
    {
      "question": "What are the sub-areas within Matunga?",
      "answer": "The main micro-localities within Matunga are Matunga East, Matunga West (Matunga Road), King's Circle, Five Gardens, the Gujarati pocket, Aravali / Telang Road belt, and the Don Bosco / college zone."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the property price in Matunga?",
      "answer": "Property prices in Matunga range from ₹1.5 Cr for a 1BHK in older buildings to ₹2.8–4.0 Cr for a 2BHK near Five Gardens/King's Circle, and ₹5–8 Cr+ for premium heritage and new-tower apartments. Rental rates range from ₹35,000 to ₹1,20,000+ per month depending on the sub-area and flat size (as of May 2026)."
    },
    {
      "question": "How to commute from Matunga?",
      "answer": "Matunga is served by Central Railway (Matunga Station) and Western Railway (Matunga Road Station), plus the Harbour line at nearby King's Circle. BEST buses, the Eastern and Western Express Highways, and quick links to Dadar, Sion and BKC make it superbly connected."
    },
    {
      "question": "Which hospitals are in Matunga?",
      "answer": "Major hospitals in and near Matunga include S.L. Raheja (Fortis) Hospital (Mahim border), the nearby K.E.M. and Tata Memorial hospitals (Parel), Bhatia Hospital connections, and several private nursing homes and 24-hour clinics across Matunga East and West."
    },
    {
      "question": "Which schools and colleges are in Matunga?",
      "answer": "Matunga is an education hub with Don Bosco High School, OLPS, Ramnarain Ruia College, R.A. Podar College of Commerce, VJTI (Veermata Jijabai Technological Institute) and ICT (Institute of Chemical Technology, formerly UDCT)."
    },
    {
      "question": "How do I find the best South Indian restaurants in Matunga?",
      "answer": "Browse Mumbai96's Matunga listings, read reviews from locals and call directly. Our verified directory makes it easy."
    }
